        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(agents): register session lock helpers in vitest workers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nVitest worker environments do not consistently set `process.env.VITEST` while `session-write-lock.ts` is evaluated. The test-only helper registration can therefore be skipped, causing unrelated node compact shards to fail on an undefined `sessionWriteLockTestApi`.\n\nProduction behavior is unchanged. The test-only guard also recognizes the repository's Vitest worker markers: `VITEST_MODE`, `VITEST_POOL_ID`, and `VITEST_WORKER_ID`.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact rebased head: `d66ad97cfe54af917e60e4c94fba9740e1d71a0d`\n\n- `oxfmt --check --threads=1 src/agents/session-write-lock.ts` passed.\n- `oxlint src/agents/session-write-lock.ts` passed.\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` passed.\n- Normal and `VITEST_POOL_ID=1` gateway suites both passed: 2 files / 17 tests.\n",
